```bash lucio command=execute show_source=false stdout=false stderr=false
# hidden block to ensure a certain queue is playing
volumito playlist play "volumito test qobuz multiple albums"
```

## Playlists

```markdown lucio command=include path="./inc/NOTE_ON_PLAYLIST_CONCEPT.md" style=literal
```

### List All Playlists

The `playlist list` command prints the identifiers
of all the available playlists:

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito playlist list
```

### Play A Playlist

To play a playlist (from its first track),
replacing the current playback queue,
issue the `playlist play` command followed by the playlist identifier:

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito playlist play "volumito test qobuz multiple albums"
```

> [!TIP]
> You might want to use double quotes if the identifier
> of the playlist contains spaces or other special characters.

### Playlist Help

These are all the subcommands of the `playlist` group:

```bash lucio command=execute
volumito playlist --help
```

The `download` subcommand is described
in Section [Download](#download) below.

The other subcommands to edit playlists are described
in Section [Edit Playlists](#edit-playlists) below.
